    {
      "id": "KA-C108-movement",
      "sequence": 4395,
      "title": "ಶಾಲೆಗೆ (śālege) — to school, not from school",
      "headword": "ನಾನು ಶಾಲೆಗೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತೇನೆ.",
      "romanization": "nānu śālege hōguttēne",
      "gloss": "I go to school — towards, not from",
      "script": "kannada",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:e0760d797681b913",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say the Kannada for “I”, “go”, “school”, “in front”, “in the middle” and “road”. Now say the answer you already know: “I have come from Bengaluru.” One direction is already yours."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: a destination",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Listen first, then say this one short sentence:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಾನು ಶಾಲೆಗೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತೇನೆ. nānu śālege hōguttēne. — “I go to school.”"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You know ಶಾಲೆ (śāle, school) and ಹೋಗು (hōgu, go). In this fixed sentence, ಶಾಲೆಗೆ (śālege) means “to school”: -ಗೆ points to the destination. Keep ಹೋಗುತ್ತೇನೆ as the whole “I go” form here. This is one place-and-verb frame, not a promise that you can attach -ಗೆ to every noun or conjugate every verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar lens: to and from",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಾನು ಶಾಲೆಗೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತೇನೆ. (nānu śālege hōguttēne) — I go to school. ನಾನು ಬೆಂಗಳೂರಿನಿಂದ ಬಂದಿದ್ದೇನೆ. — I have come from Bengaluru."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The destination ends in -ಗೆ; the starting place ends in -ಇಂದ. You already learned the whole Bengaluru answer. Listen for the difference, then say each sentence once. Do not swap “to” and “from”."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "“I go to school” in Kannada, without looking.",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: “I go to school” in Kannada, without looking.]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "“I have come from Bengaluru” in Kannada, without looking.",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: “I have come from Bengaluru” in Kannada, without looking.]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "ಶಾಲೆಗೆ from memory, then check the printed word.",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: **ಶಾಲೆಗೆ** from memory, then check the printed word.]"
            }
          ]
        },
